Integration
→ Memory Internal Storage

Device
→ Core AI Internal State

These boundaries prevent responsibility leakage.

==================================================
27. SINGLE AUTHORITY PRINCIPLE
==================================================

Each major decision must have a clear owner.

Intent interpretation:

Core AI

Routing:

Intelligence Router

Context:

Context subsystem

Persistence:

Memory

Knowledge retrieval:

Knowledge subsystem

Permission:

Governance / Privacy & Security

Execution:

iRiel System

Verification:

Verification

Interaction:

iRiel

No two layers should independently own the same architectural decision.

==================================================
28. NO INTERNAL STATE ACCESS
==================================================

A subsystem must never directly access the private state of another subsystem.

Forbidden:

Core AI
→ Memory Database

Preferred:

Core AI
→ Memory Contract
→ Memory Service
→ Internal Storage

The internal implementation remains encapsulated.

==================================================
29. EXPLICIT CONTRACTS
==================================================

Every important subsystem interface should define:

- Request.
- Identity.
- Context.
- Authorization.
- Payload.
- Expected result.
- Error state.
- Trace identifier.
- Security requirements.
- Privacy requirements.

Contracts provide predictable communication.

==================================================
30. CAPABILITY CONTRACT EXAMPLE
==================================================

Capability:

Messaging

Contract:

INPUT:
recipient
message

REQUIRES:
messaging.permission

OUTPUT:
execution_id

STATES:
SUCCESS
FAILED
DENIED
UNKNOWN

VERIFICATION:
delivery_status

The Router does not need to know whether the underlying implementation is:

- Apple Messages.
- WhatsApp.
- Telegram.
- Signal.
- Another authorized provider.

